<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Shell on cesun.life</title><link>https://example.org/zh-cn/tags/shell/</link><description>Recent content in Shell on cesun.life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 Dec 2024 18:04:45 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/zh-cn/tags/shell/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Bash</title><link>https://example.org/zh-cn/bash/</link><pubDate>Mon, 23 Dec 2024 18:04:45 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/zh-cn/bash/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Bash 既是交互式命令语言，也是脚本运行时。可靠的
shell code treats words, exit statuses, and file descriptors as distinct data
flows. Start scripts with an explicit interpreter when Bash features are
required:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;bash&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#!/usr/bin/env bash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;bash -c 'commands' name arg1&lt;/code&gt; assigns &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;$0&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;arg1&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;$1&lt;/code&gt;.
That detail matters when a command string consumes positional parameters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="shell-语法与执行"&gt;
 Shell 语法与执行
 &lt;a href="#shell-%e8%af%ad%e6%b3%95%e4%b8%8e%e6%89%a7%e8%a1%8c" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A list joins pipelines with &lt;code&gt;;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;||&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;||&lt;/code&gt; are
short-circuit operators; &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt; starts an asynchronous list. A pipeline joins
commands with &lt;code&gt;|&lt;/code&gt;, or with &lt;code&gt;|&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt; when the left command&amp;rsquo;s standard error is also
sent to the pipe.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>